{"id": "e9b861b9-834c-43f0-9bf7-293bc03cab67", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"text": "I'll check this for you. I'll look at the Bedrock invocation logging setup and the last 14 days of Bedrock activity in us-east-1. Then I'll work out which calls use a direct model ID and which use an inference profile.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "tooluse_jAhQWFDaDcfYWWJMITq1r5", "tool_name": "subagent", "input": {"name": "bedrock-model-id-check", "agent_type": "generic", "preloaded_skills": ["searching-logs", "investigating-infrastructure-changes", "exploring-metrics"], "prompt": "{
  "task": "Determine whether any Amazon Bedrock inference calls in us-east-1 over the last 14 days used a direct foundation-model ID (e.g. anthropic.claude-3-5-sonnet-20241022-v2:0, amazon.nova-pro-v1:0) where an inference profile (system-defined like us.* / global.* or application inference profile ARN) should be used instead. Report per caller (IAM principal / role / app) and per model: call counts by direct model ID vs inference profile ID/ARN.",
  "context": "User asks: 'Are any of our Bedrock calls in us-east-1 using a direct model ID where we should be using an inference profile? Check the last 14 days.' Work is read-only. Approach hints: (1) check bedrock get_model_invocation_logging_configuration in us-east-1 to see if invocation logging to CloudWatch Logs or S3 is enabled and over what period; if so query the modelId field in those logs (Logs Insights stats count(*) by modelId, identity.arn) for the last 14 days. (2) Check CloudTrail (via the lookup tool) for Bedrock events — note InvokeModel/Converse are data events and may not appear in management-event lookup; if CloudTrail data event selectors/trails exist for Bedrock, use them and say so. (3) Use CloudWatch AWS/Bedrock metrics (ModelId dimension; inference-profile ids show with profile prefix) for invocation counts per model as a supplementary signal. (4) List inference profiles (list_inference_profiles) and note which models in use have a system-defined profile available and any that REQUIRE a profile (on-demand not supported with direct ID, which would be throttle/ValidationException errors). Be explicit about data gaps (e.g. logging disabled means no per-call evidence) rather than guessing.",
  "resources": ["region us-east-1", "account 123456789012", "Bedrock runtime", "CloudWatch namespace AWS/Bedrock"],
  "timeframe": "2026-11-09T21:20:00Z/2026-11-23T21:20:00Z",
  "criteria": "Return: which models/callers use direct model IDs, which use inference profiles, volume of each, whether a system-defined profile exists for each direct-ID model, and clearly state what evidence source was used and its limits."
}"}, "type": "tool_use", "display_intent": "Check Bedrock model ID usage in us-east-1 over 14 days"}], "created_at": null}

